bayonetta 3 has been one of the most  anticipated games for nintendo switch  for several years it was announced way  back in 2017 at the game awards and  since then all we've gotten were ports  of the first two games  we finally got to see the game in action  in summer 2021 assuring us that it  wasn't vaporware but still most of the  game's features remained a complete  mystery that is until recently when  bayonetta 3 finally got a release date  and some shiny new info for fans to  feast on here's what we know about  bayonetta 3 so far  in bayonetta 3 the umbra witch teams up  with some familiar faces as well as a  new one named viola in order to put an  end to the terror of the mysterious evil  known as homunculi these new baddies are  considered man-made bio-weapons and  according to viola any hope for  defeating them lies with a scientist  named sigurd as far as who viola is very  little is still known but the release  date trailer does hint at a connection  between the character and luca  but i'm sure we'll have plenty of time  to uncover everything about viola as she  is a playable character that wields a  sword and has a cat companion named  cheshire aside from luca some of those  other familiar faces you can expect to  see include jean roden and enzo and  that's pretty much all we've been given  in terms of plot as developer platinum  games has remained tight-lipped about  many details for years however we can  confirm some of the locations players  will visit in bayonetta 3 which include  tokyo and china as for why the game's  main character is taking out enemies in  the middle of the shibuya district fans  have their theories but we'll have to  wait for the official word from platinum  before diving into all of that now fans  of the bay neta series should be very  familiar with moves like witch time and  torture attack but july's release date  trailer also teased a few new mechanics  that are sure to please one of which is  called the demon masquerade a move that  allows bayonetta to unleash even more  magic power by fusing with an infernal  demon you can only masquerade as this  demon for a short time but it sure does  look powerful the other is called demon  slave in this move lets bayonetta  control demons from a distance for some  welcome to help in battle this feature  is different yet similar to the  summoning of bayonetta 1 and 2. it even  features some familiar demons like  gamora or malthus a major new addition  to the bayonetta series is what platinum  games has named naive angel mode and  according to the company it is a  revolutionary feature that will allow  more people to fully enjoy it while the  mode is off bayonetta will be fully nude  with more sensitive areas of course  covered up by her magic hair whereas  when the mode is on she'll simply be  wearing her full outfit and the mode  does not just affect bayonetta in the  release date reveal trailer we see a  scantily clad butterfly demon also get a  bit more clothing to help make things a  bit less risque on twitter platinumgame  said by turning it on you can play right  in the living room without having to  worry about what's on screen  we think bayonetta 3 is being directed  by yusuke miata who previously served as  a game designer on astral chain despite  that game releasing two years after  bayonetta 3's original announcement in a  blog post explaining his approach to  directing the game miata said he aims to  make bayonetta control exactly how the  player wants her to  creating action connected directly to  the brain it's an important aspect of  the first two titles as well  particularly with how it rewards  perfectly timed dodges hideki kamiya who  directed the original game is the  executive producer on bayonetta 3. he is  still responsible for overseeing the  world and story in the game prior to his  time at platinum games he worked on the  devil may cry series and resident evil  2. when it comes to the voice of  bayonetta it seems fans may have to get  used to someone other than series  veteran helena taylor fans have been  quick to point out the differences with  the voice in the new trailers and many  are hoping this bayonetta is just a  younger version or one from another  universe with helena's making an  appearance at some point in the story  bayonetta 3 will be released on october  28 60 bucks like its predecessor  bayonetta 3 will be published by  nintendo thus making it an exclusive for  the switch  on twitter the original game's director  revealed platinum games wouldn't mind  having the game on other platforms but  that decision is in nintendo's hands the  first bayonetta was a multi-platform  game that originally didn't release on  nintendo's system at all however  bayonetta 2 was a wii u exclusive  because the game would not exist without  nintendo's publishing the first game is  also finally getting a physical release  on switch on september 30th alongside  the release date for part 3. nintendo  has also announced that there will be a  special edition of the game called the  trinity masquerade edition that comes  with a 200 page art book and three  reversible game cases more details will  be announced later according to the  nintendo store page baynetta 3 has been  rated m of course for violence blood and  gore strong language and partial nudity  makes me wonder if this game is  considered a t-game when playing in  naive angel mode though the game will  take up 15 gigs worth of space from your  switch which isn't bad if you think  about it and it supports handheld mode  tabletop mode and tv mode bayonetta 3 is  currently listed as a single player  experience but its predecessor did  feature two-player online and local  co-op so it is possible that a similar  feature could be announced for part 3 as  well bayonetta is walking on familiar  ground but also bringing new additions  like demon masquerade demon slave and  naive angel mode for fans and newcomers  alike there is still a decent amount of  time between now and october 28th so if  you're excited for bayonetta and want  all the latest info on the game make  sure you're subscribed to gamespot  [Music]
 

